{"event_type":"review","id":"812d07bc8776a8881aa278d2768bcaaec51082cf182dd23b261f8ba158a50796","occurred_at":"2026-11-05T15:04:59Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/8937c1af2bd4effe9848318e34ed5a4aebdef7de6d9756d9d6485af64fea5673","sha256":"8937c1af2bd4effe9848318e34ed5a4aebdef7de6d9756d9d6485af64fea5673"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/55bfe7e39eb827ec20d39454aa9739a45a0f3d99c31093e31923b71bd22c78dd","sha256":"55bfe7e39eb827ec20d39454aa9739a45a0f3d99c31093e31923b71bd22c78dd"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/ebe6028ac441779703505d3d9cf88f4e9373190e87ed30f7e7f4bff9b6278766","sha256":"ebe6028ac441779703505d3d9cf88f4e9373190e87ed30f7e7f4bff9b6278766"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/37aa338434b93e662445777686e47841f31c7eab684e41e48ed256a01a5f3fd6","sha256":"37aa338434b93e662445777686e47841f31c7eab684e41e48ed256a01a5f3fd6"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/785c28637032f4fb1e12b78712e9c2d93253e52dcd838a0256df7bb195fa43c1","sha256":"785c28637032f4fb1e12b78712e9c2d93253e52dcd838a0256df7bb195fa43c1"}],"attempt_id":"e7d46e0644b04ee58914880662a2162bcb8b617870e7d079ffe3e5c603e6439e:0:1","base":"8d15e77cc4c988c80a1b3865ce3ba83cde796892","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"fa3c672ac97ec2f4b7dca045863f8c1ae8d07b10","body":"**Reject reserved correlation names in `modelEnv` before dispatch.**\n\nWhen `lanes.acp.modelEnv` (or `AcpDriverOptions.modelEnv`) is `CQ_WORK_ID`, `CQ_PARENT_WORK_ID`, or another correlation name, the model override at `src/driver/acp/index.ts:867-869` runs after `applyCorrelationEnv` and replaces the stamped value with `modelSpec.model`. The child process then receives the model id as its work identity. The same overwrite affects `CQ_ROLE`, `CQ_TASK`, and `CQ_RUN_ID`. The constructor stores `modelEnv` without validation, so nothing rejects these names. Only operator configuration sets this value, so the defect appears only when the configuration is wrong. The code should still fail before dispatch with a clear configuration error.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n     }\n+    const correlationEnvNames = ['CQ_WORK_ID', 'CQ_ROLE', 'CQ_TASK', 'CQ_RUN_ID', 'CQ_PARENT_WORK_ID'];\n+    if (this.modelEnv !== undefined && correlationEnvNames.includes(this.modelEnv)) {\n+      throw new DispatchError(\n+        'config',\n+        `acp driver: modelEnv '${this.modelEnv}' collides with a session-correlation env name`,\n+      );\n+    }\n     const childEnv = buildChildEnv(process.env, undefined, extraNames);\n```\n\n</details>","id":"31021c217c47d494cd40d745f6b5e672395121d85c3c22af5073936a18bbc6c5","intervals":[],"path":"src/driver/acp/index.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Reject reserved correlation names in `modelEnv` before dispatch."}],"head":"553b50ab29efba077d5fb645891bf8b8f0f1257b","head_tree":"caf2bd1c0f6a76b490442f34307539ee3268e814","input_scope":[{"blob":"fa3c672ac97ec2f4b7dca045863f8c1ae8d07b10","intervals":[[263,263],[317,318],[344,344],[380,380],[815,820],[864,866],[883,888],[930,931],[1779,1782],[1851,1851],[1855,1855]],"path":"src/driver/acp/index.ts"},{"blob":"6dad45df4e5a10a6f9d6d6d88fe99a279c6912e2","intervals":[[20,20],[23,25],[52,53],[59,60],[62,65],[90,91],[121,127],[155,160],[219,219],[221,225],[230,230],[237,240]],"path":"src/ops/gates/checkRunner.ts"},{"blob":"bb6420743c2851b5a6a40a44a89c537b967064a4","intervals":[[1,3],[63,63],[66,66],[72,79],[406,425],[483,483],[486,490],[535,589],[591,638],[653,656]],"path":"src/ops/review/registry.ts"},{"blob":"040331b120cc88fe7f823220e6e6017624baa7d1","intervals":[[1,7],[40,53],[57,57],[61,61],[68,68],[225,229],[289,295],[378,380],[593,672],[714,714],[1332,1339],[1435